        "original_id": "a0790caa-c4c8-5e34-8371-8a3eb1e418a1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands: Big Pig, Blur\n- People: Sherine, Tony Antonaides, Neil Baker, Nick Disbray, Tim Rosewarne, Adrian Scaglione, Oleh Witer, Damon Albarn, Graham Coxon, Alex James, Dave Rowntree\n- Roles: lead vocals, percussion, vocals, harmonica, drums, keyboards, guitar, bass\n- Topics: band membership, lineup, genre, active years\n\nFacts:\n- Big Pig was an Australian funk, rock, and pop band that existed from 1985 to 1991.\n- An early Big Pig line-up included Sherine on lead vocals and percussion.\n- An early Big Pig line-up included Tony Antonaides on vocals and harmonica, Neil Baker on drums, Nick Disbray on vocals and percussion, Tim Rosewarne on vocals and keyboards, Adrian Scaglione on drums, and Oleh Witer on vocals and percussion.\n- Sherine had previously been in Editions and Bang.\n- Tim Rosewarne had previously been in Bang.\n- Oleh Witer had previously been in Bang.\n- Blur consists of Damon Albarn as singer and keyboardist, Graham Coxon as guitarist and singer, Alex James as bassist, and Dave Rowntree as drummer.",
